      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BETSY ANNE (1) finished third at her most recent outing, beaten 10 metres, in a nice return to form at Kilmore over 2180m. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Needs to be at her best to beat this field but she has the ability to mix it with them. LOVE WHO (4) has recorded two wins and two minor placings from the past five starts. Performed well once again when second at his latest appearance over 1690m at Maryborough, beaten 9 metres. Steps up a level but he is up to the task. CONNIES PRESIDENT NZ (8) found form and scored two runs back then came back to earth when he broke and finished seventh last start over 2100m at Charlton, coming home 40 metres from the winner. Can settle just behind them and wait on the sprint lane. Only needs to get things right to be in the money. CADENCE LANE (6) is worth some thought based on her third over 2190m at Shepparton two runs ago.",
